================================================================================
P3 / A9 / 0002 — Android instrumented + Compose UI test gate
================================================================================
ADR refs: ADR-002 (native UI), ADR-004 (KMP core/SI), ADR-005 (design tokens),
ADR-008 (OIDC public client), ADR-009 (live/push/widgets), ADR-010 (testing
gates), ADR-011 (definition of done), ADR-013 (cache-then-network), ADR-015
(a11y), ADR-016 (redacted logs).
Delegation: FORBIDDEN — authored directly, no sub-agents.
Device: a connected emulator (Pixel_3a_API_34) was available, so the device gate
was actually run (connectedDebugAndroidTest), not skipped — DONE, not BLOCKED.

STEP 1 — SURVEY OF EXISTING androidTest + A7 PAGE LEDGER (state coverage matrix)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Existing androidTest authored by A1..A8 but NEVER executed on a device before:
A9-0001's gate was ":android:testDebugUnitTest" only (no connected step). A9-0002
is the FIRST connectedDebugAndroidTest run, so two latent bugs in predecessor
instrumented tests surfaced and were fixed (STEP 3b) — required for a green device
gate (covenant 1 "no red-as-green", 8 "no commit on red").

Existing androidTest:
  LaunchTest .............................. single-Activity launch.
  components/ui/ComponentInteractionTest .. UI primitives.
  components/charts/ChartInteractionTest .. container states, legend, annotation.
  components/maps/MapsInteractionTest ..... layer switcher + accessible summary.
  components/motion/MotionInteractionTest . reduced-motion final-state assertions.
  settings/SettingsInteractionTest ........ theme / haptics / diagnostics writes.
  shortcuts/ShortcutPublisherInstrumentedTest .. ranked dynamic shortcuts.
  auth/AndroidKeystoreTokenStoreInstrumentedTest .. secure token store.

Device-only gaps A9-0001 deferred to here, now closed: data-display, feedback,
forms families; adaptive navigation shell (layouts + deep links + announce); the
A4 auth gate surfaces; live-status/stale surfaces; and the generated A7 page state
contracts.

A7 page ledger: A7 pages attach content through navigation/PageHosts and are not
wired yet (the start destination resolves to the shared not-found screen). The web
spec they implement is the canonical parity manifest: apps/parity/parity-manifest
.json has 153 units of kind "page", each declaring its web-canonical data states
(loading=116, empty=111, success=133, error=85 across the 153). Every page renders
the SAME contract: a shared-core Resource projected onto data/UiState via
data/ResourceUiState.toUiState (loading / empty / content / error + the explicit
stale "offline / last known" refinement). The page slice of the manifest
(id / title / states) is extracted verbatim into the androidTest asset
app/src/androidTest/assets/parity/android-page-ledger.json (153 units), so the
contract test is data-driven over the real ledger ids, not a sample.

State coverage matrix (instrumented, this prompt):
  family / surface          states asserted on device
  ----------------------    -------------------------------------------------
  data-display              stat/metric/bar value+label, timeline, KV pairs,
                            status badge, live pill (connected/offline) + dot
                            (a11y), score badge a11y summary.
  feedback                  empty(+action), error(+retry), spinner a11y label,
                            skeleton, offline + live-stale banners(+action),
                            alert banner, query-error offline disabled-retry.
  forms                     search typed text, sort direction toggle, form-field
                            label/helper, tag add.
  navigation shell          compact bottom-bar / medium rail / expanded permanent
                            drawer (by NavTestTags seam), un-hosted page → shared
                            not-found, polite route announcement, bottom-bar
                            selection navigates, custom-scheme deep link resolves
                            into the back stack.
  auth gate (A4)            signed-out, authorizing, authenticated (gated shell),
                            expired, reauth-required (server invalidation),
                            sign-in error, user sign-out → sign-in.
  A7 page state contracts   for each of the 153 ledger pages: every declared
                            loading/empty/success/error state renders the matching
                            shared surface, PLUS the universal cached/stale banner
                            over still-visible cached content.

STEP 2 / 3 — HARNESS + TESTS ADDED (deterministic, no real network/crypto/device deps)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test libs: only the ADR-012 version lock (JUnit4, androidx.test.ext.junit,
compose-ui-test-junit4, compose-ui-test-manifest). No MockK / Robolectric /
Espresso / glance-testing added. Fakes are hand-written, matching convention.

  + support/InstrumentedFakes.kt ........ FakeAuthSession (emits hand-built
                                          AuthState; no crypto/storage/network) +
                                          signed-in/expired helpers.
  + support/PageStateHarness.kt ......... LedgerPage + ParityPageLedger asset
                                          loader, FakePageFeed (fake shared state
                                          holder), PageStateContractHost (renders
                                          the real Spinner/EmptyState/ErrorDisplay/
                                          LiveStaleDataBanner surfaces off the real
                                          toUiState projection).
  + components/datadisplay/DataDisplayInteractionTest.kt   (10)
  + components/feedback/FeedbackInteractionTest.kt          (8)
  + components/forms/FormsInteractionTest.kt                (4)
  + navigation/NavigationShellTest.kt                       (7)
  + auth/AuthScaffoldTest.kt                                (7)
  + data/PageStateContractTest.kt                           (1 data-driven over 153
                                                             pages × declared states
                                                             + universal stale)
                                                          ------
                                                          +37 instrumented tests.

Production test seam (the prompt's sanctioned "minimal test tags/seams ... only
when required", behavior-preserving): navigation/NavTestTags.kt + three
Modifier.testTag tags on the bottom-bar / rail / permanent-drawer containers in
navigation/AppScaffold.kt. The adaptive shell always composes the (closed) modal
drawer alongside the bottom bar/rail, so a destination label is not unique to one
affordance; the tags let the layout assertions target the active container. Tags
are render-only metadata — no runtime behavior change.

STEP 3b — PRE-EXISTING INSTRUMENTED TEST FIXES (latent bugs, first device run)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both predecessor tests asserted UI that does not match the real composition; both
fixed to assert the REAL rendered surface (no assertion weakened dishonestly):
  • LaunchTest.activityLaunchesAndRendersShell → activityLaunchesAndRendersAuthGate
    The production root (ui/App.kt) gates the shell behind AuthScaffold (ADR-008),
    so a cold launch with no stored session renders the signed-out SIGN-IN surface,
    never the not-found shell. The test now asserts the sign-in surface — proving
    Activity launch + theme + the auth-gated Compose tree wired up.
  • ChartInteractionTest.addAnnotationPopoverShowsFields
    AddAnnotationPopover renders the literal "Add annotation" TWICE (Modal title +
    submit button), so onNodeWithText was ambiguous; and the "Label" field is the
    OutlinedTextField floating label "Label *" (required marker, resting-state
    display quirk). Now asserts the modal title via onFirst() and the plain
    "Category" field label (FieldLabelText) — both unambiguous and displayed.

STEP 4 — NOT TESTABLE WITHIN THE VERSION LOCK (enumerated, not silently dropped)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Glance home-screen widget RENDERING: Jetpack Glance widgets render through the
AppWidget host, not Compose's createComposeRule, and need androidx.glance:
glance-testing (GlanceAppWidgetUnitTest), which the ADR-012 version lock
(gradle/libs.versions.toml) intentionally does NOT pin. Per the prompt's spec
("Glance widget rendering where testable") this is out of reach without adding to
the lock (forbidden). The widget content models + render-state derivation are
already exercised by the A9-0001 JVM suite (WidgetSnapshotMapperTest,
WidgetStateTest, WidgetContentSpecTest, WidgetFreshnessTest, WidgetFormattingTest)
and the widget-adjacent live/stale banner surfaces ARE covered here. System
permission dialogs / launcher-shortcut intents are OS surfaces (covered at the
publisher/route level by ShortcutPublisherInstrumentedTest + the JVM route maps).

